4:T4ee,<p>Delhi is a city of contrasts, where centuries of history unfold alongside the energy and elegance of modern India. Exploring Old Delhi is an immersion into the sights, sounds and aromas of the Mughal capital. A ride on the Rickshaw through the lively lanes of Chandni Chowk, where spice merchants, traditional shops and street-food stalls bring the old city vividly to life. Visit the magnificent Jama Masjid and the imposing Red Fort, reminders of the grandeur of the Mughal emperors, and discover quiet corners where layers of Delhi’s past remain woven into everyday life.<br><br>A short distance away, New Delhi presents a very different character. Planned during the British Raj, its broad tree-lined avenues, elegant colonial buildings and formal gardens reflect the ambitions of the imperial capital. Highlights include India Gate, the impressive government buildings around Raisina Hill and the atmospheric avenues of Lutyens’ Delhi.<br><br>Together, Old and New Delhi offer a fascinating introduction to India: a city where Mughal splendour, colonial history and contemporary life exist side by side. It is this remarkable mixture of heritage, colour and everyday energy that makes Delhi such a compelling beginning to a journey through India.</p>0:{"buildId":"KT_iEaCN6K7u2oDiIQ-tU","rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","main",null,{"className":"w-full min-h-screen flex flex-col bg-background","children":[["$","$L2",null,{}],["$","$L3",null,{"galleryKey":"place-new-and-old-delhi","fallbackTitle":"New and Old Delhi","fallbackImage":"https://captivationgindia.bvox.in/storage/places/3q9waDNJb1iZWlescjsZor6JpC7IctRR1Cbzrerq.jpg"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 pt-8","children":["$","nav",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/destinations","className":"hover:text-primary transition-colors","children":"Destinations"}],[["$","span",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/des